{"id":"7319fc1b-4ea8-473d-956f-f5d5c568261d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"226d1e92875e1f4e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-codehike.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"8901c22988df7aebfdf1ff358f40cc14931b597d","start":15566,"end":15631},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","foldedHeader","=","header","?.","folded","===","true","?","header",":","undefined"]},"context":{"before":"b75a4e2189a0e7fd","after":"555044a8b8ea2742"}},"payload":{"text":"A folded block collapses to `{ ⋯ }` on the opening line: the code already ends with `{`, so we append the\nellipsis and a synthetic closing brace (the real `}` row is hidden), and clicking it unfolds the block.\nThe `folded` class switches the cell to `white-space: normal` (see git-panel.css) so the trailing newline\nInnerLine emits collapses — otherwise `pre-wrap` breaks the mark onto its own line. That collapse also\ntrims the leading indent, so a folded row keeps `margin-left` for the indent but drops the (now-moot,\nwrap-only) negative `text-indent`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:32.326Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:32.326Z"}
